{"world_id":"wld_tidal_conservatories","characters":[{"id":"chr_marenka_oyelaran","name":"Marenka Oyelaran","role":"protagonist","description":"A twenty-six-year-old junior tide-warden, the youngest to pass the lock examinations in a decade. She is lean and sunburnt, with silt-stained forearms, a braided cord of reed fiber at her wrist and a brass sounding-line she never lets out of reach. She grew up on the Mangrove Terraces, where her mother tended silt-traps, and she remembers the stories of the Great Silting from the terrace elders.","home_location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","faction_id":"fac_tide_wardens","motivation":"To keep the tide flowing so the terraces that raised her never go hungry as they did in the Lean Years.","goal":"Persuade the guilds to halt the glassblowing season so the Glassgate sills can be dredged before the spring tide.","flaw":"She trusts raw measurements over people and dismisses anyone who cannot read her data, which makes her blunt and easy to ignore.","internal_conflict":"She wants to be taken seriously as a warden but fears that raising the alarm early and being wrong will end her career.","external_conflict":"The Glassblower Guild's long firing season, protected by the Kiln Calendar dispute, blocks the shutdown she needs.","arc":"She begins as a data-bound junior who presents sounding logs to elders and is brushed off. After Guildmaster Ysolde Brandt dismisses her figures at the Quay, she carries a silted sill sample from the locks to the bell foundry and has the glassblowers feel the grit themselves, framing the problem in their own craft. She ends as a persuasive, collaborative leader who builds consensus instead of just citing numbers.","personality_traits":["precise","earnest","stubborn","observant","impatient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Tide-table reading","description":"Reads sill depth, current and the tide tables to predict flow weeks ahead.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Lock mechanics","description":"Operates and repairs vitrified gate mechanisms and sluice winches.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Sounding by line","description":"Judges silt depth by feel with a brass sounding-line, even in murky water.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_ysolde_brandt","name":"Ysolde Brandt","role":"antagonist","description":"Guildmaster of the Glassblower Guild, in her sixties, with scarred hands, a silver-streaked braid tied up in a leather wrap, and a voice made gravelly by decades at the kiln mouth. She holds the charter for every bell and window and believes the guild's survival rests on its calendar.","home_location_id":"loc_bellmakers_quay","faction_id":"fac_glassblower_guild","motivation":"To protect the guild's commissions, apprentices' livelihoods and the charter that her predecessors fought to secure.","goal":"Keep the full firing season running to complete the season's bell and window orders.","flaw":"Pride in tradition makes her treat every warning as a challenge to guild authority.","internal_conflict":"She suspects the wardens may be right but cannot reconcile halting the season with her duty to her guild's workers.","external_conflict":"The Kiln Calendar dispute pits her guild against the Tide Wardens, who need the gates shut for dredging.","arc":"She starts as a firm opponent who refuses a pause in the firing. When Marenka puts a handful of gritty sill silt in her palm and she recalls the Great Silting stories of the Lean Years, she is forced to confront the risk. She ends by proposing a staged kiln shutdown to the guild council, trading rigid pride for stewardship.","personality_traits":["proud","shrewd","protective","weathered"],"abilities":[{"name":"Guild oratory","description":"Sways guild assemblies with measured authority and precedent.","category":"social"},{"name":"Master glassworking","description":"Reads glass temperature and flaw patterns by colour and sound.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_tobias_wren","name":"Tobias Wren","role":"supporting","description":"Senior tide-warden in his fifties with a heavy frame, a grey-flecked beard and a limp from a lock winch accident. He has served at the Glassgate Locks for thirty years and trained under the warden who dug out the gates after past silting.","home_location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","faction_id":"fac_tide_wardens","motivation":"To see the locks he has served all his life passed safely to the next generation.","goal":"Guide Marenka and secure formal Warden backing for an early dredge.","flaw":"Caution hardens into inaction; he waits for certainty others cannot afford to wait for.","internal_conflict":"He wants to back Marenka but fears being blamed for an expensive false alarm at the end of his career.","external_conflict":"The Wardens' council expects proof, and the Kiln Calendar dispute with the guild limits what he can order.","arc":"He begins as a hesitant mentor who tells Marenka to wait for the official survey. After he walks the sills at low tide and sees the silt for himself, he stands with her before the Wardens' council and signs the early dredge order, ending as an active advocate rather than a cautious bystander.","personality_traits":["patient","gruff","loyal","cautious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Dredge planning","description":"Organises dredge crews and silt hauling schedules.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Institutional memory","description":"Recalls decades of lock records and past silting patterns.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_joss_halloran","name":"Joss Halloran","role":"supporting","description":"Quick-talking head of a Ferry Cooperative barge crew in his thirties, with a wind-tanned face, rope-scarred palms and a patched sail-cloth coat. He hauls harvest, glass and dredged silt across the lagoon from the Algae Fields.","home_location_id":"loc_algae_fields","faction_id":"fac_ferry_cooperative","motivation":"To secure fair earnings and a share of the rich silt for his crew's families.","goal":"Win the Cooperative's claim to dredged silt in exchange for hauling it during an emergency dredge.","flaw":"Opportunism: he bargains over every favour and loses allies' trust.","internal_conflict":"He wants to be seen as dependable but habitually puts his crew's profit ahead of the common good.","external_conflict":"The Silt Rights conflict puts the Cooperative against the Tide Wardens, who say the silt belongs to the terrace commons.","arc":"He starts by demanding payment in silt before lending barges. When the silt-debt rule means he must spread silt on the Mangrove Terraces within a season, and Marenka invites him to see the terraces' dry silt-traps, he commits his barges to the emergency dredge, ending as a trusted partner who accepts the terrace commons' share.","personality_traits":["charming","opportunistic","resourceful","restless"],"abilities":[{"name":"Barge handling","description":"Pilots sail and paddle barges through shallow, silted channels.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Haggling","description":"Negotiates deals and hauling contracts quickly.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_perpetua_sol","name":"Perpetua Sol","role":"supporting","description":"Terrace elder in her seventies, small and wiry with white hair under a woven reed hat and hands stained green from root-gardens. She keeps the oral memory of the Great Silting and Marenka's mother was her apprentice.","home_location_id":"loc_mangrove_terraces","motivation":"To make sure the terraces never again suffer hunger as in the Lean Years.","goal":"Mobilise terrace families to take part in the dredge and receive the silt back.","flaw":"She distrusts guilds and wardens alike and rarely shares her authority.","internal_conflict":"She wants to pass knowledge on, but fears her community's old grievances will block cooperation.","external_conflict":"The Silt Rights dispute threatens the terraces' claim to the silt that would restore their soil.","arc":"She begins as a wary elder who withholds terrace labour from outside authorities. After Marenka brings her the sill samples and the Great Silting records match what Perpetua remembers, she calls the terrace families to join the dredge beside wardens and ferry crews, ending as a bridge between factions rather than a gatekeeper.","personality_traits":["wise","wary","dry-humoured","stubborn"],"abilities":[{"name":"Oral history","description":"Recounts the Great Silting and its lessons with precise detail.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Silt-trap tending","description":"Reads soil and silt quality and manages root-garden silt traps.","category":"other"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_marenka_ysolde_rivalry","source_character_id":"chr_marenka_oyelaran","target_character_id":"chr_ysolde_brandt","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Marenka Oyelaran presses Ysolde Brandt to halt the firing season, and Ysolde treats the young warden's warnings as an affront to guild authority, creating the central clash of the Kiln Calendar."},{"id":"rel_ysolde_marenka_dismissal","source_character_id":"chr_ysolde_brandt","target_character_id":"chr_marenka_oyelaran","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Ysolde Brandt dismisses Marenka Oyelaran as an inexperienced junior and uses the guild's charter to block her appeals."},{"id":"rel_tobias_marenka_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_tobias_wren","target_character_id":"chr_marenka_oyelaran","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Tobias Wren trained Marenka Oyelaran at the locks, but his caution to wait for the survey slows her urgent push for an early dredge."},{"id":"rel_joss_tobias_dispute","source_character_id":"chr_joss_halloran","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_wren","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Joss Halloran bargains with Tobias Wren over who owns dredged silt, mirroring the Silt Rights conflict between the Ferry Cooperative and the Tide Wardens."},{"id":"rel_perpetua_marenka_kin","source_character_id":"chr_perpetua_sol","target_character_id":"chr_marenka_oyelaran","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Perpetua Sol, who trained Marenka Oyelaran's mother, offers the terrace elder's memory of the Great Silting as evidence but withholds terrace labour until she is convinced."},{"id":"rel_joss_perpetua_silt","source_character_id":"chr_joss_halloran","target_character_id":"chr_perpetua_sol","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Joss Halloran wants the rich dredged silt for his Ferry Cooperative crews, while Perpetua Sol insists it belongs on the terraces, sharpening the Silt Rights dispute."}]}
