 tide-warden in his fifties with a heavy frame, a grey-flecked beard and a limp from a lock winch accident. He has served at the Glassgate Locks for thirty years and trained under the warden who dug out the gates after past silting.","home_location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","faction_id":"fac_tide_wardens","motivation":"To see the locks he has served all his life passed safely to the next generation.","goal":"Guide Marenka and secure formal Warden backing for an early dredge.","flaw":"Caution hardens into inaction; he waits for certainty others cannot afford to wait for.","internal_conflict":"He wants to back Marenka but fears being blamed for an expensive false alarm at the end of his career.","external_conflict":"The Wardens' council expects proof, and the Kiln Calendar dispute with the guild limits what he can order.","arc":"He begins as a hesitant mentor who tells Marenka to wait for the official survey. After he walks the sills at low tide and sees the silt for himself, he stands with her before the Wardens' council and signs the early dredge order, ending as an active advocate rather than a cautious bystander.","personality_traits":["patient","gruff","loyal","cautious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Dredge planning","description":"Organises dredge crews and silt hauling schedules.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Institutional memory","description":"Recalls decades of lock records and past silting patterns.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_joss_halloran","name":"Joss Halloran","role":"supporting","description":"Quick-talking head of a Ferry Cooperative barge crew in his thirties, with a wind-tanned face, rope-scarred palms and a patched sail-cloth coat. He hauls harvest, glass and dredged silt across the lagoon from the Algae Fields.","home_location_id":"loc_algae_fields","faction_id":"fac_ferry_cooperative","motivation":"To secure fair earnings and a share of the rich silt for his crew's families.","goal":"Win the Cooperative's claim to dredged silt in exchange for hauling it during an emergency dredge.","flaw":"Opportunism: he bargains over every favour and loses allies' trust.","internal_conflict":"He wants to be seen as dependable but habitually puts his crew's profit ahead of the common good.","external_conflict":"The Silt Rights conflict puts the Cooperative against the Tide Wardens, who say the silt belongs to the terrace commons.","arc":"He starts by demanding payment in silt before lending barges. When the silt-debt rule means he must spread silt on the Mangrove Terraces within a season, and Marenka invites him to see the terraces' dry silt-traps, he commits his barges to the emergency dredge, ending as a trusted partner who accepts the terrace commons' share.","personality_traits":["charming","opportunistic","resourceful","restless"],"abilities":[{"name":"Barge handling","description":"Pilots sail and paddle barges through shallow, silted channels.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Haggling","description":"Negotiates deals and hauling contracts quickly.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_perpetua_sol","name":"Perpetua Sol","role":"supporting","description":"Terrace elder in her seventies, small and wiry with white hair under a woven reed hat and hands stained green from root-gardens. She keeps the oral memory of the Great Silting and Marenka's mother was her apprentice.","home_location_id":"loc_mangrove_terraces","motivation":"To make sure the terraces never again suffer hunger as in the Lean Years.","goal":"Mobilise terrace families to take part in the dredge and receive the silt back.","flaw":"She distrusts guilds and wardens alike and rarely shares her authority.","internal_conflict":"She wants to pass knowledge on, but fears her community's old grievances will block cooperation.","external_conflict":"The Silt Rights dispute threatens the terraces' claim to the silt that would restore their soil.","arc":"She begins as a wary elder who withholds terrace labour from outside authorities. After Marenka brings her the sill samples and the Great Silting records match what Perpetua remembers, she calls the terrace families to join the dredge beside wardens and ferry crews, ending as a bridge between factions rather than a gatekeeper.","personality_traits":["wise","wary","dry-humoured","stubborn"],"abilities":[{"name":"Oral history","description":"Recounts the Great Silting and its lessons with precise detail.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Silt-trap tending","description":"Reads soil and silt quality and manages root-garden silt traps.","category":"other"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_marenka_ysolde_rivalry","source_character_id":"chr_marenka_oyelaran","target_character_id":"chr_ysolde_brandt","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Marenka Oyelaran presses Ysolde Brandt to halt the firing season, and Ysolde treats the young warden's warnings as an affront to guild authority, creating the central clash of the Kiln Calendar."},{"id":"rel_ysolde_marenka_dismissal","source_character_id":"chr_ysolde_brandt","target_character_id":"chr_marenka_oyelaran","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Ysolde Brandt dismisses Marenka Oyelaran as an inexperienced junior and uses the guild's charter to block her appeals."},{"id":"rel_tobias_marenka_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_tobias_wren","target_character_id":"chr_marenka_oyelaran","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Tobias Wren trained Marenka Oyelaran at the locks, but his caution to wait for the survey slows her urgent push for an early dredge."},{"id":"rel_joss_tobias_dispute","source_character_id":"chr_joss_halloran","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_wren","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Joss Halloran bargains with Tobias Wren over who owns dredged silt, mirroring the Silt Rights conflict between the Ferry Cooperative and the Tide Wardens."},{"id":"rel_perpetua_marenka_kin","source_character_id":"chr_perpetua_sol","target_character_id":"chr_marenka_oyelaran","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Perpetua Sol, who trained Marenka Oyelaran's mother, offers the terrace elder's memory of the Great Silting as evidence but withholds terrace labour until she is convinced."},{"id":"rel_joss_perpetua_silt","source_character_id":"chr_joss_halloran","target_character_id":"chr_perpetua_sol","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Joss Halloran wants the rich dredged silt for his Ferry Cooperative crews, while Perpetua Sol insists it belongs on the terraces, sharpening the Silt Rights dispute."}]}
