 rigging and rooftops with near-weightless steps, though never over open water.","category":"supernatural"},{"name":"Reed-Marsh Swordwork","description":"A swift, economical style of short cuts and sidesteps learned in the marshes of the Thunder Reed Dojo.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Tally-Reading","description":"Can read the notches and cord-knots of a master's tally-stick and the sects it names.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_chen_yuhe","name":"Chen Yuhe","role":"supporting","description":"A forty-year-old Crane Sect covenant-witness at Bannerhall, a heavyset, soft-spoken man with ink-darkened sleeves and a crane-shaped seal at his belt. He has recorded every formal challenge for fifteen years and knows each precedent by heart. He once knew Master Hu Bairen as a correspondent and rival at the game of covenant law.","home_location_id":"loc_bannerhall","faction_id":"fac_crane_sect","motivation":"To keep the Crane Banner pact alive, because he watched the Net Wars' aftermath as a boy and fears the covenant's collapse.","goal":"Find a legal reading that makes the tally-stick binding without breaking the covenant's own forms.","flaw":"He hides behind procedure and precedent, and so delays decisive action while people suffer.","internal_conflict":"He loves the covenant's letter but suspects its spirit demands that he defy his superiors.","external_conflict":"The Crane Sect's senior keepers, caught in the Unanswered Tally deadlock, forbid him to acknowledge Mei's stick.","arc":"He begins as a cautious clerk who shelters behind precedent. When Mei appears at Bannerhall with the tally and the Crane elders order him to refuse it, he must choose between his post and the pact's purpose. He enters the stick into the covenant record on his own seal, accepting censure. He ends as a witness who acts on principle rather than waiting for permission.","personality_traits":["meticulous","gentle","cautious","scholarly"],"abilities":[{"name":"Covenant Law","description":"Deep command of dueling precedent and the pact's formal procedure.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Witness's Authority","description":"His seal and testimony carry weight at Bannerhall and with neutral parties.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_dao_shenhai","name":"Dao Shenhai","role":"antagonist","description":"A fifty-year-old master of the Eel School, broad-shouldered and scarred across the knuckles, with salt-stiffened hair braided in the school's eel-knot. His family's boats were burned in the Net Wars, and he has built his whole school on the vow that the rookery shallows will never again be lost to others.","home_location_id":"loc_mist_rookery","faction_id":"fac_eel_school","motivation":"To secure the rookery shallows so his school's families never go hungry as his own once did.","goal":"Keep the tally-stick from binding the Eel School and win the right to fish the rookery shallows.","flaw":"His fear of scarcity makes him treat every compromise as the first step toward ruin.","internal_conflict":"He knows the nesting ban protects the eel grounds he wants, yet he cannot let go of the grievance that defines him.","external_conflict":"The Crane Sect's nesting ban and Mei's tally-stick both threaten to bind his school to a moot he fears.","arc":"He begins as a hardliner who sees the tally as a trap. Facing Mei in a formal challenge at Bannerhall, he finds his champion's ambush plan would repeat the Broken Challenge, the shame of which he despises. He calls the ambush off and answers the challenge honestly, losing the duel but gaining a hearing. He ends reluctantly willing to send an envoy, his grievance loosened by the realization that fishing out the rookery would doom his own people.","personality_traits":["proud","fierce","wary","disciplined"],"abilities":[{"name":"Eel-Knot Grappling","description":"Slippery close-range style of locks and twisting escapes.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Commanding Presence","description":"His school follows him with unwavering loyalty.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_ruo_ximen","name":"Ruo Ximen","role":"supporting","description":"A thirty-year-old Salt Warden captain on Saltmarket Isle, wiry and sharp-eyed, wearing a salt-white coat and a brass whistle. She mediates disputes among envoys and has seen the market peace tested often since the Broken Challenge's stories were told to her as a child.","home_location_id":"loc_saltmarket_isle","faction_id":"fac_salt_wardens","motivation":"To guard the market peace that feeds her island and honor the oath her wardens swore after the Broken Challenge.","goal":"Ensure every envoy who comes to Saltmarket Isle leaves alive and unharmed, including Mei.","flaw":"She is rigidly neutral and refuses to take a side even when one is plainly in the right.","internal_conflict":"She believes neutrality keeps the peace, but starts to suspect that it also lets the feud grow.","external_conflict":"Eel School hotheads press her to hand Mei over, and the Crane Sect presses her to eject her.","arc":"She begins as a warden who holds her neutrality as an unbreakable creed. When Eel School agents demand Mei's surrender at the market, she must decide whether neutrality means giving a hunted envoy up. She invokes the market peace to protect Mei and publicly declares the tally-stick a lawful envoy's token. She ends understanding that guarding the peace sometimes means acting for it.","personality_traits":["blunt","fair-minded","watchful","pragmatic"],"abilities":[{"name":"Safe-Conduct Authority","description":"Can invoke the market peace to shield envoys on Saltmarket Isle.","category":"social"},{"name":"Whistle Signals","description":"Coordinates the wardens quickly across the market with whistle codes.","category":"other"}]},{"id":"chr_hu_bairen","name":"Hu Bairen","role":"supporting","description":"The late master of the Thunder Reed Dojo, seen in memory and through his tally-stick. He was a gaunt, white-bearded swordsman who kept cranes in the marsh and taught that a