command of dueling precedent and the pact's formal procedure.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Witness's Authority","description":"His seal and testimony carry weight at Bannerhall and with neutral parties.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_dao_shenhai","name":"Dao Shenhai","role":"antagonist","description":"A fifty-year-old master of the Eel School, broad-shouldered and scarred across the knuckles, with salt-stiffened hair braided in the school's eel-knot. His family's boats were burned in the Net Wars, and he has built his whole school on the vow that the rookery shallows will never again be lost to others.","home_location_id":"loc_mist_rookery","faction_id":"fac_eel_school","motivation":"To secure the rookery shallows so his school's families never go hungry as his own once did.","goal":"Keep the tally-stick from binding the Eel School and win the right to fish the rookery shallows.","flaw":"His fear of scarcity makes him treat every compromise as the first step toward ruin.","internal_conflict":"He knows the nesting ban protects the eel grounds he wants, yet he cannot let go of the grievance that defines him.","external_conflict":"The Crane Sect's nesting ban and Mei's tally-stick both threaten to bind his school to a moot he fears.","arc":"He begins as a hardliner who sees the tally as a trap. Facing Mei in a formal challenge at Bannerhall, he finds his champion's ambush plan would repeat the Broken Challenge, the shame of which he despises. He calls the ambush off and answers the challenge honestly, losing the duel but gaining a hearing. He ends reluctantly willing to send an envoy, his grievance loosened by the realization that fishing out the rookery would doom his own people.","personality_traits":["proud","fierce","wary","disciplined"],"abilities":[{"name":"Eel-Knot Grappling","description":"Slippery close-range style of locks and twisting escapes.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Commanding Presence","description":"His school follows him with unwavering loyalty.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_ruo_ximen","name":"Ruo Ximen","role":"supporting","description":"A thirty-year-old Salt Warden captain on Saltmarket Isle, wiry and sharp-eyed, wearing a salt-white coat and a brass whistle. She mediates disputes among envoys and has seen the market peace tested often since the Broken Challenge's stories were told to her as a child.","home_location_id":"loc_saltmarket_isle","faction_id":"fac_salt_wardens","motivation":"To guard the market peace that feeds her island and honor the oath her wardens swore after the Broken Challenge.","goal":"Ensure every envoy who comes to Saltmarket Isle leaves alive and unharmed, including Mei.","flaw":"She is rigidly neutral and refuses to take a side even when one is plainly in the right.","internal_conflict":"She believes neutrality keeps the peace, but starts to suspect that it also lets the feud grow.","external_conflict":"Eel School hotheads press her to hand Mei over, and the Crane Sect presses her to eject her.","arc":"She begins as a warden who holds her neutrality as an unbreakable creed. When Eel School agents demand Mei's surrender at the market, she must decide whether neutrality means giving a hunted envoy up. She invokes the market peace to protect Mei and publicly declares the tally-stick a lawful envoy's token. She ends understanding that guarding the peace sometimes means acting for it.","personality_traits":["blunt","fair-minded","watchful","pragmatic"],"abilities":[{"name":"Safe-Conduct Authority","description":"Can invoke the market peace to shield envoys on Saltmarket Isle.","category":"social"},{"name":"Whistle Signals","description":"Coordinates the wardens quickly across the market with whistle codes.","category":"other"}]},{"id":"chr_hu_bairen","name":"Hu Bairen","role":"supporting","description":"The late master of the Thunder Reed Dojo, seen in memory and through his tally-stick. He was a gaunt, white-bearded swordsman who kept cranes in the marsh and taught that a duel is a conversation. He wrote the tally-stick's notches himself in his final winter.","home_location_id":"loc_thunder_reed_dojo","motivation":"To end the feud before the cranes are lost, as a last act of care for the coast.","goal":"Have his tally-stick carried to the three sects through the one student he trusts most.","flaw":"He chose silence over explanation, leaving Mei to bear the elders' anger without understanding his reasons.","internal_conflict":"He feared that naming a disowned-to-be student as heir would break his school, yet he trusted no one else.","external_conflict":"His own dojo elders opposed his peace plan and sought to bury the tally-stick after his death.","arc":"He begins, in memory, as a master who keeps his plan secret to protect his school. His pivotal choice is to hand Mei the tally-stick before the elders can seize it, accepting that she will be disowned for it. Through Mei's journey, his hidden plan becomes known and his school's elders are shamed into listening. He ends as a remembered teacher whose silence is forgiven and whose peace is finally carried out.","personality_traits":["wise","secretive","gentle","patient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Master Swordsman","description":"Taught a refined style built on restraint and timing.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Crane-Keeping","description":"Raised cranes in the marsh and read their behavior as omens.","category":"other"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_hu_mei_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_hu_bairen","target_character_id":"chr_mei_lanying","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Hu Bairen raised and trained Mei Lanying, and entrusted her with the tally-stick, a trust that cost her her place at the Thunder Reed Dojo."},{"id":"rel_mei_dao_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_mei_lanying","target_character_id":"chr_dao_shenhai","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Mei Lanying's tally-stick would bind Dao Shenhai's Eel School to a moot he opposes, so he works to stop her."},{"id":"rel_chen_mei_ally","source_character_id":"chr_chen_yuhe","target_character_id":"chr_mei_lanying","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Chen Yuhe, once a correspondent of Hu Bairen, secretly aids Mei Lanying's claim against his own sect's orders."},{"id":"rel_ruo_mei_protector","source_character_id":"chr_ruo_ximen","target_character_id":"chr_mei_lanying","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Ruo Ximen guarantees Mei Lanying's safe conduct on Saltmarket Isle, though she insists she does so only as the market's neutral warden."},{"id":"rel_dao_chen_rival","source_character_id":"chr_dao_shenhai","target_character_id":"chr_chen_yuhe","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Dao Shenhai distrusts Chen Yuhe as the Crane Sect's witness, whose rulings have repeatedly favored the nesting ban over the Eel School's claim."}]}
