{"world_id":"wld_perihelion_yard","characters":[{"id":"chr_maren_okafor","name":"Maren Okafor","role":"protagonist","description":"A forty-one-year-old salvage rigger with sixteen years on the Yard Spine. She is wiry and sun-scarred, with a burn-mottled left forearm from a heat-budget overrun. She grew up on a tanker-cannibal crew and learned to read hull logs the way others read faces. She wears a patched thermal suit stamped with her union roster number.","motivation":"She needs proof that the logs she has trusted all her career are honest, because her late partner was blamed for a ledger discrepancy that she now suspects was staged.","goal":"Document the power draw of the hull logged as scrapped and file it with the Charter Audit Office before the auditors arrive.","flaw":"She works alone and hides half-finished evidence, believing no one else will protect it as carefully as she does.","internal_conflict":"She wants vindication for her partner, but she fears the hull may show he really did divert salvage.","external_conflict":"Her heat budget is nearly spent, and the mass ledger makes her own recovery of the hull's data technically theft if she logs it wrong.","arc":"Maren starts out hoarding evidence and distrusting everyone. Her pivotal moment comes when the union's heat roster would bar her from the sunside hull, and she must hand her raw telemetry to Teodor Brandt to get a shift swap. She then files a joint, fully logged claim and ends the story trusting a shared record over private proof.","personality_traits":["stubborn","meticulous","laconic","guarded"],"abilities":[{"name":"Hull Log Forensics","description":"She spots falsified duty and mass entries from timestamp drift and inconsistent decimal habits.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Sunside Rigging","description":"She works efficiently in extreme heat, managing her thermal budget to the minute.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Power Trace Rig","description":"She improvises sensors to detect trickle power draw from a dormant hull.","category":"technological"}],"home_location_id":"loc_yard_spine","faction_id":"fac_riggers_union"},{"id":"chr_teodor_brandt","name":"Teodor Brandt","role":"supporting","description":"A fifty-three-year-old union heat-roster steward with a ledger-keeper's stoop and a voice worn thin from decades of arguing shifts. He keeps a paper backup of every roster. He sat on the committee that rewrote the safety charter after the Sail Fire.","motivation":"He wants no more riggers cooked by schedules, as the Sail Fire killed his brother.","goal":"Hold Helio Tank to the heat budget and keep the roster law intact.","flaw":"He is rigidly procedural and refuses any bend in the rules, even ones that would save a rigger.","internal_conflict":"He values the law he helped write but suspects that it is now being used to bury the truth about scrapped hulls.","external_conflict":"Helio Tank pushes him for longer sunside shifts while the union membership accuses him of obstruction.","arc":"Brandt begins as a stickler who denies shift exceptions. Maren's telemetry shows a hull drawing power in a place that thermal survey cannot see, which makes him realize the heat budget is being gamed. He signs a one-time roster exception on his own authority and ends the story willing to break procedure to protect riggers.","personality_traits":["rigid","honest","weary","protective"],"abilities":[{"name":"Roster Law","description":"He knows the charter and duty log precedents well enough to win or block any shift dispute.","category":"social"},{"name":"Heat Budget Modelling","description":"He projects safe sunside exposure for a crew from sail geometry and orbit phase.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_mirror_shed","faction_id":"fac_riggers_union"},{"id":"chr_ilse_varga","name":"Ilse Varga","role":"antagonist","description":"A forty-six-year-old Helio Tank yard liaison with a shaved head, immaculate grey coveralls, and a calm, courteous manner. She has run the scrap purchasing desk for twelve years and keeps the quiet spares of the yard in Shadow Dock off the books.","motivation":"She believes that keeping spare hulls hidden keeps the yard solvent and protects the jobs of hundreds of riggers.","goal":"Keep the hull in Shadow Dock off the ledger and discredit Maren before the auditors arrive.","flaw":"She is convinced that her intentions excuse her methods, so she cannot see her deceptions as harmful.","internal_conflict":"She sincerely believes she is protecting the yard, yet each cover-up requires harming the riggers she claims to protect.","external_conflict":"The Charter Audit Office is days from arrival and Maren's power trace could expose her hidden spares.","arc":"Varga starts out as a composed manager who hides spares for the yard's sake. She orders the Shadow Dock power cut, and that act puts Maren's heat budget at risk and exposes the hull's thermal signature. When it fails she gives the auditors a full accounting, ending the story as someone who must answer for her choices.","personality_traits":["composed","paternalistic","strategic","polite"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger Manipulation","description":"She reroutes mass entries through scrap purchase records so unlogged hulls look scrapped.","category":"social"},{"name":"Shadow Dock Access","description":"She holds the berthing keys and survey blind-spot schedules for the eclipsed dock.","category":"other"}],"home_location_id":"loc_shadow_dock","faction_id":"fac_helio_tank"},{"id":"chr_dov_Auditor_placeholder","name":"Placeholder","role":"supporting","description":"x","motivation":"x","goal":"x","flaw":"x","internal_conflict":"x","external_conflict":"x","arc":"x","home_location_id":"loc_bastion_hulk"}],"relationships":[]}

