 purchasing desk for twelve years and keeps the quiet spares of the yard in Shadow Dock off the books.","motivation":"She believes that keeping spare hulls hidden keeps the yard solvent and protects the jobs of hundreds of riggers.","goal":"Keep the hull in Shadow Dock off the ledger and discredit Maren before the auditors arrive.","flaw":"She is convinced that her intentions excuse her methods, so she cannot see her deceptions as harmful.","internal_conflict":"She sincerely believes she is protecting the yard, yet each cover-up requires harming the riggers she claims to protect.","external_conflict":"The Charter Audit Office is days from arrival and Maren's power trace could expose her hidden spares.","arc":"Varga starts out as a composed manager who hides spares for the yard's sake. She orders the Shadow Dock power cut, and that act puts Maren's heat budget at risk and exposes the hull's thermal signature. When it fails she gives the auditors a full accounting, ending the story as someone who must answer for her choices.","personality_traits":["composed","paternalistic","strategic","polite"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger Manipulation","description":"She reroutes mass entries through scrap purchase records so unlogged hulls look scrapped.","category":"social"},{"name":"Shadow Dock Access","description":"She holds the berthing keys and survey blind-spot schedules for the eclipsed dock.","category":"other"}],"home_location_id":"loc_shadow_dock","faction_id":"fac_helio_tank"},{"id":"chr_dov_halloran","name":"Dov Halloran","role":"supporting","description":"A thirty-eight-year-old senior auditor of the Charter Audit Office with a permanent berth at the Bastion Hulk. He is lean and pale from years in shielded modules, and he carries a stylus-worn slate of every ledger he has reconciled.","motivation":"He wants to prove the audit office still catches fraud, since the Audit Charter was born from a season of ledger fraud and his reputation rests on its purpose.","goal":"Reconcile the mass ledger against physical hull counts before the audit closes.","flaw":"He trusts documents over people and dismisses any claim that lacks a ledger entry.","internal_conflict":"He needs to believe the ledger is the truth, yet he suspects its entries have been quietly edited.","external_conflict":"Helio Tank pressures the audit office to close quickly, and a tight-beam reply from the inner system takes at least ten minutes, so he cannot get instant direction from superiors.","arc":"Halloran begins as a clerk who accepts only logged evidence. Maren's power trace contradicts a scrapped entry, and he must choose whether to accept unlogged physical data. He walks the Shadow Dock himself and ends the story trusting measured reality alongside the ledger.","personality_traits":["precise","skeptical","fair","cautious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger Reconciliation","description":"He cross-checks mass entries against hull counts to find discrepancies.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Audit Authority","description":"He is empowered to seize the mass ledger and freeze yard transfers.","category":"social"}],"home_location_id":"loc_bastion_hulk","faction_id":"fac_charter_audit"}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_maren_brandt_ally","source_character_id":"chr_maren_okafor","target_character_id":"chr_teodor_brandt","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Maren Okafor relies on Teodor Brandt, her union steward, for the heat roster exception she needs, but his procedural rigidity and her secrecy keep them at odds."},{"id":"rel_varga_maren_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_ilse_varga","target_character_id":"chr_maren_okafor","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Ilse Varga works to discredit and sideline Maren Okafor because Maren's power trace threatens the hidden spare hulls in Shadow Dock."},{"id":"rel_halloran_maren_rival","source_character_id":"chr_dov_halloran","target_character_id":"chr_maren_okafor","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Dov Halloran treats Maren Okafor's unlogged evidence with suspicion and could charge her with theft, even as her findings point to the fraud he is meant to find."},{"id":"rel_brandt_varga_rival","source_character_id":"chr_teodor_brandt","target_character_id":"chr_ilse_varga","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Teodor Brandt resists Ilse Varga's push for longer sunside shifts on behalf of Helio Tank, and the two clash over the heat budget."}]}

