rs alone on the road.","goal":"Keep the dilution hidden through the circuit and pin the Cut Grain on the Millers' Compact.","flaw":"He believes his own lies are justified by need, and he grows careless whenever he feels cornered.","internal_conflict":"He cannot reconcile his oath to the keepers with his belief that the order will let the valleys starve.","external_conflict":"Maren's public testing threatens to expose him, and the keepers' rule strikes adulterers from the rolls.","arc":"Edric begins by deflecting suspicion with small, plausible accusations toward the Compact. When Maren proposes the open sack test at Ford Market, he tries to switch a sack and is caught by Tobin's weigh-house seal. He ends struck from the rolls, his name never to be carried again.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","anxious","resentful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Persuasion","description":"Makes accusations sound like reasonable concern.","category":"social"},{"name":"Account Juggling","description":"Hides losses by shifting numbers between caravan and vault tallies.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_wren_tally","name":"Wren Tally","role":"supporting","description":"A sixteen-year-old apprentice keeper with a gap-toothed grin and an oversized coat inherited from a dead cousin. Orphaned in the last hard winter, she was taken in by the order and assigned to Maren's wagon. She keeps a notched stick to count every sack.","home_location_id":"loc_granary_hill","faction_id":"fac_seed_keepers","motivation":"She wants to belong to something that will not abandon her, and the order is the only home she has.","goal":"Earn her keeper's knot by completing the circuit without losing a single sack.","flaw":"She is overeager to please and keeps quiet when she notices something wrong.","internal_conflict":"She admires Edric, who taught her to count, yet her tally stick keeps disagreeing with his totals.","external_conflict":"Edric pressures her to accept his numbers while Maren expects her to speak up about errors.","arc":"Wren begins by hiding the mismatch between her tally and Edric's, afraid of losing her place. Before the Frost Gate she brings the notched stick to Maren and testifies against him. She ends as a keeper who speaks first when the count is wrong.","personality_traits":["earnest","observant","anxious","quick-witted"],"abilities":[{"name":"Tally Notching","description":"Keeps exact running counts on a notched stick without error.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Light-Footed Scouting","description":"Moves quietly and scouts ahead of the caravan on narrow trails.","category":"physical"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_maren_edric_suspicion","source_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","target_character_id":"chr_edric_cole","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Maren Voss trusts her quartermaster Edric Cole as a fellow keeper and relies on his accounts, which blinds her to his dilution of the stock and deepens the Cut Grain feud."},{"id":"rel_edric_tobin_blame","source_character_id":"chr_edric_cole","target_character_id":"chr_tobin_hale","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Edric Cole steers blame for the Cut Grain toward Tobin Hale and the Millers' Compact, inflaming the old distrust between keepers and millers."},{"id":"rel_maren_tobin_distrust","source_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","target_character_id":"chr_tobin_hale","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Maren Voss and Tobin Hale begin as wary rivals over the weigh-house ledgers, each assuming the other's order is cheating the tithe, before they slowly become partners."},{"id":"rel_sorrel_maren_claim","source_character_id":"chr_sorrel_ashby","target_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Sorrel Ashby accuses Maren Voss of carrying the orchard families' promised grafting stock away, threatening to block the caravan on the orchard road."},{"id":"rel_maren_wren_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","target_character_id":"chr_wren_tally","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Maren Voss mentors her apprentice Wren Tally, pressing her to speak up about errors, which collides with Wren's loyalty to Edric."},{"id":"rel_wren_edric_loyalty","source_character_id":"chr_wren_tally","target_character_id":"chr_edric_cole","relationship_type":"friend","description":"Wren Tally admires Edric Cole, who taught her to count, and her loyalty makes her hide the mismatch between her tally stick and his totals."}]}
