 stooped and silver-haired, who tends the sealed stacks of the Lamp Archive. Her hands are scarred by lamp-oil and she has not left the stacks in four counts. She wears her lamp on a chain and treats it as part of her body.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_lamp_archive","faction_id":"fac_lamplighters","motivation":"She wants to protect the sealed pages and the Kin's standing from any hint that the archive can be breached.","goal":"Keep the sealed ledgers closed until a proper weigher's warrant is delivered, and keep her lamp and post.","flaw":"Fear of losing her lamp makes her inflexible and unwilling to take any risk, even for a good cause.","internal_conflict":"She knows a sealed page may hold the proof of a wrong, but speaking of it aloud would cost her everything she has.","external_conflict":"The lamp-oath forbids reading sealed pages aloud, and the Sealed Ledgers dispute leaves her demanding a warrant that the weighers are slow to give.","arc":"Begins as a keeper who will not open or discuss any sealed page. Once Marrow's warrant is signed, she is asked to confirm the page's contents out loud. She chooses to point at the entry and let Ilse read it herself, honouring the oath while still providing the third key. She ends willing to act within her rules rather than hide behind them.","personality_traits":["cautious","dutiful","quiet","watchful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Lamplight Reading","description":"Can find any entry in the sealed stacks by the glow of her lamp, without opening the ledgers unnecessarily.","category":"supernatural"},{"name":"Archive Memory","description":"Remembers the shelving order of thousands of ledgers of the long dead.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_corvane_dray","name":"Corvane Dray","description":"A senior scribe and supervisor of Ilse's desk in the Counting Halls, round-faced and affable, with ink-black fingers and a ready smile. He rose by smoothing disputes rather than settling them, and keeps a private ledger of favours.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_counting_halls","faction_id":"fac_scribes_order","motivation":"He wants to avoid being the scribe whose desk produced the miscast tally, since it would end his advancement.","goal":"Keep the correction quiet by quietly re-columning the soul's entry himself, so no audit ever reaches the Weighers.","flaw":"Cowardice disguised as pragmatism; he buries problems instead of facing them.","internal_conflict":"He once took pride in accurate work and cannot reconcile that with the shortcuts he now takes.","external_conflict":"The Miscast Harvest puts his desk under scrutiny and Ilse's correction threatens to prove the error began on his watch.","arc":"Starts as Ilse's friendly mentor who tries to bury the error. When Ilse refuses his offer of a quiet re-columning in front of other scribes, his scheme collapses and he is forced to either confirm her hand or be exposed. He grudgingly signs the scribe's key, ending as a man who accepts the cost of his own mistake.","personality_traits":["genial","evasive","ambitious","persuasive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Smooth Talk","description":"Defuses arguments and wins favours by seeming reasonable and helpful.","category":"social"},{"name":"Favour Ledger","description":"Keeps track of debts owed across the Counting Halls and calls them in when needed.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_pell_ostrander","name":"Pell Ostrander","description":"A tally-clerk at the Gate of Receipts who stamps arriving souls' slips and queues them for weighing. Young-looking, restless, with a habit of tapping his stamp against the counter. He remembers every soul he has stamped by the sound of their name.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_gate_of_receipts","faction_id":"fac_scribes_order","motivation":"He wants to be promoted out of the Gate into the Counting Halls and sees helping Ilse as a way to prove himself.","goal":"Delay the misplaced soul's place in the weighing queue long enough for Ilse to complete the three keys.","flaw":"Impulsive and boastful; he promises more than he can deliver.","internal_conflict":"He wants the credit of a rescue but fears being blamed if it fails.","external_conflict":"Altering the queue breaks Gate procedure and the Miscast Harvest puts every stamp under review.","arc":"Starts eager to impress and willing to bend the queue for glory. When Corvane threatens to have his stamp revoked, he must decide whether to withdraw or keep the soul's slip in the queue. He keeps it there and takes the blame openly, ending as a clerk who values the work above the recognition.","personality_traits":["restless","boastful","loyal","quick-witted"],"abilities":[{"name":"Queue Control","description":"Can reorder and hold the arrival queue within the Gate's routine without drawing notice.","category":"other"},{"name":"Name Memory","description":"Recalls every soul's name and slip number after a single hearing.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_ilse_corvane_supervision","source_character_id":"chr_ilse_quillfane","target_character_id":"chr_corvane_dray","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Corvane Dray supervises Ilse Quillfane's desk and acts as her mentor, but his wish to bury the miscast tally turns his guidance into pressure against her correction."},{"id":"rel_corvane_ilse_suppression","source_character_id":"chr_corvane_dray","target_character_id":"chr_ilse_quillfane","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Corvane Dray treats Ilse Quillfane as a threat to his career and works to quietly re-column the soul's entry before her correction reaches the Weighers."},{"id":"rel_ilse_marrow_petition","source_character_id":"chr_ilse_quillfane","target_character_id":"chr_marrow_vesk","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Ilse Quillfane must petition Marrow Vesk for the weigher's key and warrant, while Marrow's pride in the Collegium makes him resist her claim of an error."},{"id":"rel_marrow_teodra_warrant","source_character_id":"chr_marrow_vesk","target_character_id":"chr_teodra_ashwick","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Teodra Ashwick refuses to open the sealed ledgers without a warrant from Marrow Vesk, and Marrow's reluctance to sign it deadlocks the Sealed Ledgers dispute."},{"id":"rel_pell_ilse_ally","source_character_id":"chr_pell_ostrander","target_character_id":"chr_ilse_quillfane","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Pell Ostrander helps Ilse Quillfane by holding the misplaced soul's slip in the queue at the Gate, risking his stamp to buy her time."},{"id":"rel_teodra_ilse_oath","source_character_id":"chr_teodra_ashwick","target_character_id":"chr_ilse_quillfane","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Teodra Ashwick bound by her lamp-oath, can only point to the sealed entry and trust Ilse Quillfane to read it, becoming her reluctant ally for the third key."}]}
