ar-old master founder and Wren's teacher, broad and stooped, with a cracked leather apron and a grey beard stained by bronze dust. He cast the fifth bell of the wall and has led the foundry for three decades. He is hiding an old, unfinished casting in the back of the foundry.","home_location_id":"loc_founder_row","faction_id":"fac_bell_founders","motivation":"To protect the Collegium's name and his foundry's life's work from a treason charge.","goal":"Keep the unmarked bell's origin secret until he can prove it was not cast on his orders.","flaw":"Pride that makes him lie rather than admit a failure.","internal_conflict":"He loves Wren like a daughter but fears her truth-seeking will destroy the Collegium he serves.","external_conflict":"The Watch's writs threaten the foundry, and treason under the nine-bell law carries forfeiture of his mark.","arc":"Corvin begins by denying the tenth bell and deflecting Wren's questions. When the watch arrives at Founder Row with a writ and searches his foundry, he is forced to show Wren the abandoned casting he made years ago. He ends by confessing before the Collegium and accepting the cost of his pride.","personality_traits":["proud","gruff","protective","secretive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Master caster","description":"Decades of expertise in bronze casting and bell tuning.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Collegium standing","description":"His word still sways the founders' council.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_ishbel_marrow","name":"Warden Ishbel Marrow","role":"antagonist","description":"A forty-year-old warden of the Parish Watch with a rigid bearing, a long grey coat and a silver writ-case at her belt. She lost her sister to the Chiming and has written the silence laws' strictest clauses herself. She reads writs on Bailiff's Stairs each dawn.","home_location_id":"loc_bailiffs_stairs","faction_id":"fac_parish_watch","motivation":"To make sure no one else loses a name to fog, whatever it costs.","goal":"Silence the bells by writ and prove the Collegium cast the tenth bell.","flaw":"Rigid conviction: she mistakes procedure for safety and cannot bear ambiguity.","internal_conflict":"She suspects the tenth ring might protect people, but admitting it would mean her sister's loss was avoidable.","external_conflict":"The founders resist her writs, and the Fog Brokers' name-debts undermine her authority over the parish.","arc":"Ishbel begins as an unyielding enforcer of the writ. When Wren brings her a recording of the ninth stroke speaking a salt-registered name during fog, she hears a lost name returned and cannot deny it. She ends by suspending the silencing order and letting the bells ring under watch oversight.","personality_traits":["disciplined","grieving","exacting","incorruptible"],"abilities":[{"name":"Writ authority","description":"Can still a bell and compel testimony by watch writ.","category":"social"},{"name":"Interrogation","description":"Reads evasions in a witness's pauses.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_pell_vantrook","name":"Pell Vantrook","role":"supporting","description":"A thirty-year-old licensed Fog Broker, thin and elegant, in a lamp-oil-scented waistcoat with a charter badge pinned beside a dozen tokens of others' names. He holds name-debts on much of the parish, including Corvin's apprentices, and works the Fogmarket stalls.","home_location_id":"loc_fogmarket","faction_id":"fac_fog_brokers","motivation":"To grow his name-debt holdings into a lasting hold over the parish council.","goal":"Buy Wren's secret about the tenth ring and sell it to whichever side pays most.","flaw":"Avarice: he prices everything, including loyalty.","internal_conflict":"He privately fears his own name was sold long ago and he has no true self to trade.","external_conflict":"The watch calls his trade extortion and is hunting for grounds to void his charter.","arc":"Pell begins as a neutral dealer who sells information to both sides. When Ishbel threatens to void the Brokers' Charter unless he testifies, he gives Wren the ledger entry that traces the tenth bell's casting. He ends by burning the name-debt he holds against her family and paying for it in lost standing.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","wary","witty"],"abilities":[{"name":"Name-trading","description":"Knows how to value, trade and hold name-debts under charter.","category":"social"},{"name":"Fogmarket contacts","description":"Network of informants across the night market.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_odalys_finch","name":"Sister Odalys Finch","role":"supporting","description":"A fifty-five-year-old keeper of the salt registry at the Salt Chapel, small and soft-spoken, with hands cracked white from salt. She has written thousands of names and remembers each hand. She has quietly found one entry with no known writer.","home_location_id":"loc_salt_chapel","motivation":"To keep every citizen's name safe in the registry she has tended for decades.","goal":"Find out who wrote the nameless entry on the salt and whether it belongs to the tenth ring.","flaw":"Timidity: she avoids confronting power and keeps secrets to avoid trouble.","internal_conflict":"She believes the registry is sacred, yet suspects its record may be wrong or altered.","external_conflict":"Both the watch and the Fog Brokers pressure her for access to the registry.","arc":"Odalys begins by hiding the anomalous entry out of fear. When Wren brings her the ninth stroke's pattern and the lost parish records match it, she opens the registry to Wren's inquiry. She ends by testifying publicly before the watch about the unmarked entry.","personality_traits":["gentle","meticulous","timid","devout"],"abilities":[{"name":"Salt-hand memory","description":"Recognises any registered hand and can spot forgeries.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_wren_corvin_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_halloway","target_character_id":"chr_wren_aldous","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Mas