s by writ and prove the Collegium cast the tenth bell.","flaw":"Rigid conviction: she mistakes procedure for safety and cannot bear ambiguity.","internal_conflict":"She suspects the tenth ring might protect people, but admitting it would mean her sister's loss was avoidable.","external_conflict":"The founders resist her writs, and the Fog Brokers' name-debts undermine her authority over the parish.","arc":"Ishbel begins as an unyielding enforcer of the writ. When Wren brings her a recording of the ninth stroke speaking a salt-registered name during fog, she hears a lost name returned and cannot deny it. She ends by suspending the silencing order and letting the bells ring under watch oversight.","personality_traits":["disciplined","grieving","exacting","incorruptible"],"abilities":[{"name":"Writ authority","description":"Can still a bell and compel testimony by watch writ.","category":"social"},{"name":"Interrogation","description":"Reads evasions in a witness's pauses.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_pell_vantrook","name":"Pell Vantrook","role":"supporting","description":"A thirty-year-old licensed Fog Broker, thin and elegant, in a lamp-oil-scented waistcoat with a charter badge pinned beside a dozen tokens of others' names. He holds name-debts on much of the parish, including Corvin's apprentices, and works the Fogmarket stalls.","home_location_id":"loc_fogmarket","faction_id":"fac_fog_brokers","motivation":"To grow his name-debt holdings into a lasting hold over the parish council.","goal":"Buy Wren's secret about the tenth ring and sell it to whichever side pays most.","flaw":"Avarice: he prices everything, including loyalty.","internal_conflict":"He privately fears his own name was sold long ago and he has no true self to trade.","external_conflict":"The watch calls his trade extortion and is hunting for grounds to void his charter.","arc":"Pell begins as a neutral dealer who sells information to both sides. When Ishbel threatens to void the Brokers' Charter unless he testifies, he gives Wren the ledger entry that traces the tenth bell's casting. He ends by burning the name-debt he holds against her family and paying for it in lost standing.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","wary","witty"],"abilities":[{"name":"Name-trading","description":"Knows how to value, trade and hold name-debts under charter.","category":"social"},{"name":"Fogmarket contacts","description":"Network of informants across the night market.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_odalys_finch","name":"Sister Odalys Finch","role":"supporting","description":"A fifty-five-year-old keeper of the salt registry at the Salt Chapel, small and soft-spoken, with hands cracked white from salt. She has written thousands of names and remembers each hand. She has quietly found one entry with no known writer.","home_location_id":"loc_salt_chapel","motivation":"To keep every citizen's name safe in the registry she has tended for decades.","goal":"Find out who wrote the nameless entry on the salt and whether it belongs to the tenth ring.","flaw":"Timidity: she avoids confronting power and keeps secrets to avoid trouble.","internal_conflict":"She believes the registry is sacred, yet suspects its record may be wrong or altered.","external_conflict":"Both the watch and the Fog Brokers pressure her for access to the registry.","arc":"Odalys begins by hiding the anomalous entry out of fear. When Wren brings her the ninth stroke's pattern and the lost parish records match it, she opens the registry to Wren's inquiry. She ends by testifying publicly before the watch about the unmarked entry.","personality_traits":["gentle","meticulous","timid","devout"],"abilities":[{"name":"Salt-hand memory","description":"Recognises any registered hand and can spot forgeries.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_wren_corvin_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_halloway","target_character_id":"chr_wren_aldous","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Master Corvin Halloway taught Wren Aldous the craft of casting and has hidden the old foundry casting from her, so his protection of her is entangled with his lies."},{"id":"rel_wren_ishbel_rival","source_character_id":"chr_ishbel_marrow","target_character_id":"chr_wren_aldous","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Warden Ishbel Marrow seeks to silence the bells and sees apprentice Wren Aldous as a witness who must be restrained, which pushes Wren to act alone."},{"id":"rel_pell_wren_broker","source_character_id":"chr_pell_vantrook","target_character_id":"chr_wren_aldous","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Pell Vantrook holds a name-debt on Wren Aldous's family and uses it to demand her findings about the tenth ring."},{"id":"rel_ishbel_pell_pressure","source_character_id":"chr_ishbel_marrow","target_character_id":"chr_pell_vantrook","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Warden Ishbel Marrow calls Pell Vantrook's name-debts extortion and threatens his charter, forcing him to choose between sides."},{"id":"rel_odalys_wren_ally","source_character_id":"chr_odalys_finch","target_character_id":"chr_wren_aldous","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Sister Odalys Finch secretly helps Wren Aldous by sharing the registry's strange entry, bound by sympathy for Wren's lost mother."},{"id":"rel_corvin_ishbel_conflict","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_halloway","target_character_id":"chr_ishbel_marrow","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Master Corvin Halloway resists Warden Ishbel Marrow's writs over the foundry, each seeing the other as the danger to the wall."}]}
