ter Corvin Halloway taught Wren Aldous the craft of casting and has hidden the old foundry casting from her, so his protection of her is entangled with his lies."},{"id":"rel_wren_ishbel_rival","source_character_id":"chr_ishbel_marrow","target_character_id":"chr_wren_aldous","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Warden Ishbel Marrow seeks to silence the bells and sees apprentice Wren Aldous as a witness who must be restrained, which pushes Wren to act alone."},{"id":"rel_pell_wren_broker","source_character_id":"chr_pell_vantrook","target_character_id":"chr_wren_aldous","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Pell Vantrook holds a name-debt on Wren Aldous's family and uses it to demand her findings about the tenth ring."},{"id":"rel_ishbel_pell_pressure","source_character_id":"chr_ishbel_marrow","target_character_id":"chr_pell_vantrook","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Warden Ishbel Marrow calls Pell Vantrook's name-debts extortion and threatens his charter, forcing him to choose between sides."},{"id":"rel_odalys_wren_ally","source_character_id":"chr_odalys_finch","target_character_id":"chr_wren_aldous","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Sister Odalys Finch secretly helps Wren Aldous by sharing the registry's strange entry, bound by sympathy for Wren's lost mother."},{"id":"rel_corvin_ishbel_conflict","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_halloway","target_character_id":"chr_ishbel_marrow","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Master Corvin Halloway resists Warden Ishbel Marrow's writs over the foundry, each seeing the other as the danger to the wall."}]}
