{"world_id":"wld_thistledown","characters":[{"id":"chr_marrow_fennick","name":"Marrow Fennick","role":"protagonist","description":"A hedge-witch tea merchant in her early forties, broad-shouldered and weathered from years on country roads, with moss-green mittens, a satchel of dried herbs, and a kettle she calls Old Patience. Her family held the Ninth Stall until a promised favour went unkept past the third bell a generation ago, and she has followed the fair every leap-season since, selling blends from a handcart at the edge of the Kettle Commons.","home_location_id":"loc_kettle_commons","faction_id":"fac_stallholders","motivation":"To restore the family name her grandmother lost and give her tea a permanent, rooted home.","goal":"Claim the Ninth Stall's lease before the third bell of closing day.","flaw":"Stubborn pride: she refuses to ask for help or admit she owes anyone anything.","internal_conflict":"She wants the stall to honour her family, but fears she is chasing an old grievance instead of building a life of her own.","external_conflict":"The Carter Kin are quietly selling the lease, and she lacks the favours and standing the Stallholders' Round requires to vote it back to her.","arc":"Marrow begins by hoarding her pride and trading only for herself. When the Carter Kin offer to buy her claim and the favour shortage threatens to ride her debts out with the fair, she must publicly accept a favour from Tamsin and promise one in return before the Tallykeepers. Having asked for help and kept her word, she ends the story as a trusted member of the Round who values the bargain more than the grievance.","personality_traits":["stubborn","warm","dry-witted","proud","observant"],"abilities":[{"name":"Hedge-blending","description":"Brews teas that soothe tempers, sharpen memory, or ease sleep using hedgerow herbs.","category":"supernatural"},{"name":"Shrewd haggling","description":"Reads a seller's tells and finds bargains that leave both sides content.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tamsin_wick","name":"Tamsin Wick","role":"supporting","description":"A freckled, ink-stained young apprentice tallykeeper of sixteen who wears a lopsided cap and carries a satchel of blank wishing tags. She grew up among the barn's rafters, memorising the fair's debts, and is quietly bothered by how many promises hang unkept.","home_location_id":"loc_wishing_barn","faction_id":"fac_tallykeepers","motivation":"To prove that tallying favours should help people keep promises, not only record failures.","goal":"Find a legitimate way to keep the Ninth Stall's old favour so the forfeit can be reconciled on the tally.","flaw":"Rigid rule-following: she hesitates to act without a precedent written down.","internal_conflict":"She loves the Tally Accord's order but suspects its strictness has hurt people like Marrow's family.","external_conflict":"Senior tallykeepers resist reopening an old forfeit while the favour shortage forces them to prioritise current debts.","arc":"Tamsin starts as a clerk who only cites precedent. When she finds the original favour's wishing tag still hanging in the barn, she must choose whether to argue a new reading of the Accord before the senior tallykeepers. She speaks up, sets a precedent that a favour may be kept by another hand, and ends as a confident tallykeeper who treats rules as tools.","personality_traits":["earnest","meticulous","shy","curious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Tag memory","description":"Recalls the wording and date of nearly any wishing tag she has read.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Careful drafting","description":"Writes bargains in plain terms that leave no loophole for either party.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_oswin_carter","name":"Oswin Carter","role":"antagonist","description":"A silver-bearded, soft-spoken elder of the Carter Kin, always wrapped in a patched travelling coat with brass bells on the hem. He has steered the wains between fields for fifty seasons and speaks of the lanes as if they were family.","home_location_id":"loc_leap_lane","faction_id":"fac_carters","motivation":"To secure funds and a lasting stall for the Carter Kin, whose wains are ageing and whose young are leaving the road.","goal":"Complete the sale of the Ninth Stall's lease before closing day.","flaw":"Quiet secrecy: he believes the Kin's needs justify withholding the truth from everyone else.","internal_conflict":"He values the fair's honour of kept promises but is breaking the spirit of it by selling a lease that is not his alone to sell.","external_conflict":"Marrow's claim and Tamsin's search of the tally threaten to expose the sale to the Stallholders' Round.","arc":"Oswin begins by hiding the sale behind courtesy. When Marrow offers a contest of trade before the Round rather than a fight, he has to reveal the Kin's wains are failing. He agrees to share the lease through a bargain that funds new wains, ending as an open ally who no longer needs secrets.","personality_traits":["courteous","secretive","patient","worn"],"abilities":[{"name":"Lane-knowing","description":"Senses where the fair's lanes will fold and unfold before others can.","category":"supernatural"},{"name":"Quiet persuasion","description":"Speaks so gently that others agree before noticing they were steered.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_bramble_hobb","name":"Bramble Hobb","role":"supporting","description":"A round, cheerful stallholder who runs the busiest tea tent in the Kettle Commons, with flour-dusted sleeves and a booming laugh. He is the Round's current voice and has traded gossip with Marrow for a dozen seasons.","home_location_id":"loc_kettle_commons","faction_id":"fac_stallholders","motivation":"To keep the Round fair and the Commons friendly so his own trade stays steady.","goal":"Hold a calm vote on the Ninth Stall that does not split the Round.","flaw":"Conflict-avoidance: he smooths over problems rather than confronting them.","internal_conflict":"He likes Marrow and suspects the Carter sale is crooked, but fears losing the Kin's goodwill and the wains that carry his stock.","external_conflict":"The Round is divided over the lease, and the favour shortage makes every member guard their own debts.","arc":"Bramble begins by joking away rumours about the sale. When Marrow's contest forces the Round to vote openly, he must break the tie himself. He votes to hear both claims in full and ends as a Round speaker who names problems early.","personality_traits":["jovial","generous","evasive","gossipy"],"abilities":[{"name":"Crowd-calming","description":"Defuses heated arguments with humour and a well-timed pot of tea.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_marrow_oswin_claim","source_character_id":"chr_marrow_fennick","target_character_id":"chr_oswin_carter","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Marrow Fennick and Oswin Carter are rivals over the Ninth Stall's lease; she holds the family claim while he is quietly selling it, so each stands in the other's way."},{"id":"rel_oswin_marrow_guilt","source_character_id":"chr_oswin_carter","target_character_id":"chr_marrow_fennick","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Oswin Carter privately respects Marrow Fennick's persistence but sees her claim as the one obstacle to the Kin's survival, so he delays and deflects her."},{"id":"rel_tamsin_marrow_ally","source_character_id":"chr_tamsin_wick","target_character_id":"chr_marrow_fennick","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Tamsin Wick quietly helps Marrow Fennick search the wishing tags, and their bargain forces Marrow to accept help while Tamsin risks her standing with the senior tallykeepers."},{"id":"rel_bramble_marrow_friend","source_character_id":"chr_bramble_hobb","target_character_id":"chr_marrow_fennick","relationship_type":"friend","description":"Bramble Hobb is an old trading friend of Marrow Fennick, but his reluctance to take sides strains their friendship as the Round's vote nears."},{"id":"rel_bramble_oswin_trade","source_character_id":"chr_bramble_hobb","target_character_id":"chr_oswin_carter","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Bramble Hobb depends on Oswin Carter's wains to carry his stock, which makes him slow to question Oswin's sale of the Ninth Stall."}]}
