social"}]},{"id":"chr_tamsin_wick","name":"Tamsin Wick","role":"supporting","description":"A freckled, ink-stained young apprentice tallykeeper of sixteen who wears a lopsided cap and carries a satchel of blank wishing tags. She grew up among the barn's rafters, memorising the fair's debts, and is quietly bothered by how many promises hang unkept.","home_location_id":"loc_wishing_barn","faction_id":"fac_tallykeepers","motivation":"To prove that tallying favours should help people keep promises, not only record failures.","goal":"Find a legitimate way to keep the Ninth Stall's old favour so the forfeit can be reconciled on the tally.","flaw":"Rigid rule-following: she hesitates to act without a precedent written down.","internal_conflict":"She loves the Tally Accord's order but suspects its strictness has hurt people like Marrow's family.","external_conflict":"Senior tallykeepers resist reopening an old forfeit while the favour shortage forces them to prioritise current debts.","arc":"Tamsin starts as a clerk who only cites precedent. When she finds the original favour's wishing tag still hanging in the barn, she must choose whether to argue a new reading of the Accord before the senior tallykeepers. She speaks up, sets a precedent that a favour may be kept by another hand, and ends as a confident tallykeeper who treats rules as tools.","personality_traits":["earnest","meticulous","shy","curious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Tag memory","description":"Recalls the wording and date of nearly any wishing tag she has read.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Careful drafting","description":"Writes bargains in plain terms that leave no loophole for either party.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_oswin_carter","name":"Oswin Carter","role":"antagonist","description":"A silver-bearded, soft-spoken elder of the Carter Kin, always wrapped in a patched travelling coat with brass bells on the hem. He has steered the wains between fields for fifty seasons and speaks of the lanes as if they