{"world_id":"wld_comet_market","characters":[{"id":"chr_isolde_vane","name":"Isolde Vane","role":"protagonist","description":"A lean, ink-stained woman in her late thirties who serves as factotum to the Mapmakers' Guild. She wears a sun-faded guild sash over patched pilot's leathers and carries a tether-knife she has never drawn in anger. Raised in the Map House as an orphan apprentice, she grew up on the lore of the Map Wars and believes the seal is the only thing standing between the fleet and wreckage.","home_location_id":"loc_map_house","faction_id":"fac_mapmakers","motivation":"She fears a repeat of the Map Wars and wants the fleet to survive perihelion on charts everyone can trust.","goal":"Arbitrate the theft of the sealed perihelion chart in the Long Hall and get it back under seal before the burn.","flaw":"She treats the guild's rules as unquestionable and mistakes procedure for justice.","internal_conflict":"She suspects the seal system that raised her may itself endanger pilots, but doubting it feels like betraying the only family she has had.","external_conflict":"The burn articles allow no litigation through perihelion, so she has a short window to rule while guild elders and pilots both press her to favor their side.","arc":"Isolde begins as a rigid enforcer who would condemn the pilot holding the chart as a pirate. During the Long Hall hearing, the chart's holder proves the sealed route would have sent ships into the comet's plume, which forces her to use her arbiter's power under the map-seal rule to open the chart publicly. She ends as an arbiter who weighs the safety of the fleet above the letter of the seal.","personality_traits":["dry-witted","meticulous","loyal","secretly daring"],"abilities":[{"name":"Arbiter's Eye","description":"Spots forged seals, altered ink and false testimony.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Tether Running","description":"Moves quickly along docking tethers in the comet's spin.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Silver Tongue of the Hall","description":"Frames rulings under the burn articles so that both sides can accept them.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_calder_rook","name":"Calder Rook","role":"supporting","description":"A broad-shouldered free pilot with a salt-white braid and a scarred harpoon arm, captain of the sail-ship Gull's Gambit. He took the stolen chart from a fence and claims salvage rights, having flown the perihelion route twice by hand. He is charming and unrepentant, and he keeps his debts in a ledger he pretends not to read.","home_location_id":"loc_tether_docks","faction_id":"fac_free_pilots","motivation":"He wants his crew to survive the burn and wants pilots to stop flying routes drawn by people who have never flown them.","goal":"Keep the chart long enough to prove in open hall that the sealed route is deadly, and pay his ice-tithe so he keeps his tether.","flaw":"He is reckless and dodges accountability by turning every serious charge into a joke.","internal_conflict":"He knows that keeping the chart is theft, yet he cannot call it that without admitting he has become the thing he despises.","external_conflict":"The Ice Barons are buying tethers out from under pilots who owe tithes, while the guild wants him charged with piracy.","arc":"Calder starts as a smirking salvager who treats the theft as a game. When Baron Ysolt's agents move to buy his tether on the eve of the burn, he must either run with the chart or testify openly in the Long Hall. He testifies, accepting a guild penalty, and ends as a pilot who owns his actions and fights for pilots through the Compact's arbitration rights.","personality_traits":["charismatic","reckless","evasive","fiercely loyal to his crew"],"abilities":[{"name":"Plume Flying","description":"Handles reaction-plume manoeuvres through tight burn windows.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Harpoon Throw","description":"Hits distant tethers and moving targets with a harpoon.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Dockside Charm","description":"Talks his way into berths and favors.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_ysolt_marrenhal","name":"Ysolt Marrenhal","role":"antagonist","description":"An elderly Ice Baron with pale eyes and rings of frozen amber on every finger, holder of the deepest claims in the Core Vaults. She has outlived three perihelions and two rivals, and she speaks softly because she is used to being obeyed.","home_location_id":"loc_core_vaults","faction_id":"fac_ice_barons","motivation":"She wants to control which ships can leave at perihelion so that her ice claims keep their value.","goal":"Obtain the stolen chart and buy up the tethers of indebted pilots so that only her contracted ships can fly the safe route.","flaw":"Her greed makes her treat people as inventory, and she underestimates those who cannot be bought.","internal_conflict":"She is aging and afraid of dying before another orbit, and she cannot decide whether to protect her legacy or simply hoard.","external_conflict":"The Long Hall arbitration threatens to publish the route, which would erase her advantage, and the free pilots are able to expose the tether grab.","arc":"Ysolt begins as a patient collector confident she can corner the route. Her agents' attempt to seize Calder's tether is exposed during the hearing, and Isolde's ruling opens the chart to all, ending her monopoly. She ends diminished but still alive, forced to pay tithes on every tether she bought and to share the route openly.","personality_traits":["patient","calculating","courteous","ruthless"],"abilities":[{"name":"Tether Buyout","description":"Quietly purchases tether rights through proxies.","category":"social"},{"name":"Claim Law","description":"Knows every loophole in the burn articles.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_pell_odrin","name":"Pell Odrin","role":"supporting","description":"A young glasshouse grower from the Cinder Gardens, freckled and sun-reddened, who also works as a part-time courier for the Map House. He saw the chart change hands and has been carrying the knowledge like a stone in his boot.","home_location_id":"loc_cinder_gardens","faction_id":"fac_mapmakers","motivation":"He wants to stay safe and keep his family's glasshouse alive through the burn.","goal":"Decide whether to tell Isolde what he saw without ending his apprenticeship or crossing the Ice Barons.","flaw":"He freezes under pressure and lets others decide for him.","internal_conflict":"He owes loyalty to the guild that employs him but fears Baron Ysolt's retaliation against his family's claim.","external_conflict":"Ysolt's agents offer him tithe relief for silence while Isolde demands testimony in the Long Hall.","arc":"Pell starts as a frightened witness who hides what he saw. When the guild offers no protection and Ysolt's offer arrives, he is pushed to choose, and he steps into the Long Hall to name the buyer. He ends as a steadier young man who has learned that testimony can protect the Gardens better than silence.","personality_traits":["nervous","observant","earnest","gentle"],"abilities":[{"name":"Light-Reader","description":"Reads sunlight and heat to predict glasshouse yields and the burn.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Courier's Memory","description":"Remembers faces and handovers in crowded markets.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_isolde_calder_charge","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","target_character_id":"chr_calder_rook","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Isolde Vane must judge Calder Rook, who holds the stolen chart; she sees him as a pirate while he claims salvage, and the hearing forces each to question the other's view."},{"id":"rel_ysolt_calder_tether","source_character_id":"chr_ysolt_marrenhal","target_character_id":"chr_calder_rook","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Ysolt Marrenhal is buying up Calder Rook's tether through proxies to strand him and seize the chart he carries."},{"id":"rel_pell_isolde_witness","source_character_id":"chr_pell_odrin","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Pell Odrin runs messages for Isolde Vane and admires her, but fears to give her the testimony she needs about the chart's handover."},{"id":"rel_ysolt_pell_bribe","source_character_id":"chr_ysolt_marrenhal","target_character_id":"chr_pell_odrin","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Ysolt Marrenhal offers Pell Odrin tithe relief for his silence, pressuring him to conceal that her agents bought the stolen chart."}]}
