iption":"Talks his way into berths and favors.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_ysolt_marrenhal","name":"Ysolt Marrenhal","role":"antagonist","description":"An elderly Ice Baron with pale eyes and rings of frozen amber on every finger, holder of the deepest claims in the Core Vaults. She has outlived three perihelions and two rivals, and she speaks softly because she is used to being obeyed.","home_location_id":"loc_core_vaults","faction_id":"fac_ice_barons","motivation":"She wants to control which ships can leave at perihelion so that her ice claims keep their value.","goal":"Obtain the stolen chart and buy up the tethers of indebted pilots so that only her contracted ships can fly the safe route.","flaw":"Her greed makes her treat people as inventory, and she underestimates those who cannot be bought.","internal_conflict":"She is aging and afraid of dying before another orbit, and she cannot decide whether to protect her legacy or simply hoard.","external_conflict":"The Long Hall arbitration threatens to publish the route, which would erase her advantage, and the free pilots are able to expose the tether grab.","arc":"Ysolt begins as a patient collector confident she can corner the route. Her agents' attempt to seize Calder's tether is exposed during the hearing, and Isolde's ruling opens the chart to all, ending her monopoly. She ends diminished but still alive, forced to pay tithes on every tether she bought and to share the route openly.","personality_traits":["patient","calculating","courteous","ruthless"],"abilities":[{"name":"Tether Buyout","description":"Quietly purchases tether rights through proxies.","category":"social"},{"name":"Claim Law","description":"Knows every loophole in the burn articles.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_pell_odrin","name":"Pell Odrin","role":"supporting","description":"A young glasshouse grower from the Cinder Gardens, freckled and sun-reddened, who also works as a part-time courier for the Map House. He saw the chart change hands and has been carrying the knowledge like a stone in his boot.","home_location_id":"loc_cinder_gardens","faction_id":"fac_mapmakers","motivation":"He wants to stay safe and keep his family's glasshouse alive through the burn.","goal":"Decide whether to tell Isolde what he saw without ending his apprenticeship or crossing the Ice Barons.","flaw":"He freezes under pressure and lets others decide for him.","internal_conflict":"He owes loyalty to the guild that employs him but fears Baron Ysolt's retaliation against his family's claim.","external_conflict":"Ysolt's agents offer him tithe relief for silence while Isolde demands testimony in the Long Hall.","arc":"Pell starts as a frightened witness who hides what he saw. When the guild offers no protection and Ysolt's offer arrives, he is pushed to choose, and he steps into the Long Hall to name the buyer. He ends as a steadier young man who has learned that testimony can protect the Gardens better than silence.","personality_traits":["nervous","observant","earnest","gentle"],"abilities":[{"name":"Light-Reader","description":"Reads sunlight and heat to predict glasshouse yields and the burn.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Courier's Memory","description":"Remembers faces and handovers in crowded markets.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_isolde_calder_charge","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","target_character_id":"chr_calder_rook","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Isolde Vane must judge Calder Rook, who holds the stolen chart; she sees him as a pirate while he claims salvage, and the hearing forces each to question the other's view."},{"id":"rel_ysolt_calder_tether","source_character_id":"chr_ysolt_marrenhal","target_character_id":"chr_calder_rook","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Ysolt Marrenhal is buying up Calder Rook's tether through proxies to strand him and seize the chart he carries."},{"id":"rel_pell_isolde_witness","source_character_id":"chr_pell_odrin","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Pell Odrin runs messages for Isolde Vane and admires her, but fears to give her the testimony she needs about the chart's handover."},{"id":"rel_ysolt_pell_bribe","source_character_id":"chr_ysolt_marrenhal","target_character_id":"chr_pell_odrin","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Ysolt Marrenhal offers Pell Odrin tithe relief for his silence, pressuring him to conceal that her agents bought the stolen chart."}]}
