at binds both men to the unregistered gifts if Ishvari exposes them."},{"id":"rel_devaraj_ishvari_ally","source_character_id":"chr_devaraj_nayar","target_character_id":"chr_ishvari_menon","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Devaraj Nayar shares with Ishvari Menon a belief that public rite and the ledger must stay honest, and he quietly gives her the hour he expects the wind to turn so that she can finish her ruling in time."},{"id":"rel_kadir_devaraj_pressure","source_character_id":"chr_kadir_al_hamadi","target_character_id":"chr_devaraj_nayar","relationship_type":"antagonist","description":"Kadir al-Hamadi presses Devaraj Nayar through an agent for an early hint of the turning, testing the pilot's loyalty to the Ghat Oath."}]}
